ep 2: Structure for Your 8–12 Page Whitepaper (PDF)
When authoring your whitepaper in Microsoft Word, LaTeX, or Google Docs prior to exporting to PDF, structure the content across the following required sections:

Title Page & Abstract: Concise summary (~250 words) detailing background, methodology, experimental results, and key findings.

Introduction & Literature Background: Contextualizing customer churn modeling, mathematical foundations of ensemble learning algorithms, and research gaps.

Data Methodology & Exploratory Data Analysis: Data collection, distribution sanity checks, feature transformations, scaling procedures, and correlation matrices.

Predictive Modeling & Hyperparameter Selection: Algorithm choices, stratified k-fold cross-validation strategies, and loss function optimizations.

Model Evaluation & Discussion: Comparative metric analysis (Accuracy, Precision, Recall, F1-Score, ROC-AUC), feature importance rankings, and error analysis.

Business Implications & Recommendations: Translation of model outputs into actionable business strategies, target deployment workflows, and risk mitigations.

References & Code Appendix: Citations of relevant literature and complete GitHub repository link.

Implementation & Deliverable Submission Notes
Repository Setup: Organize your GitHub repository with standard structure:

/data/ — Raw and processed datasets

/notebooks/ — Clean, executed .ipynb capstone notebook

/reports/ — Exported Data Science Research Report PDF

README.md — Project summary, reproduction steps, and key findings

Submission: Paste your public GitHub Repository URL or public Google Drive PDF link into the Submit deliverable field on your dashboard.
